  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "中短篇小說賞讀",
    "sub_ename": "APPRECIATION AND READING OF NOVELLAS AND SHORT STORIES",
    "describe_ch": "本課程旨在幫助研究生於批判性地閱讀和分析中短篇小說方面，建立一個穩固的基礎。我們希望通過對中短篇小說的深入閱讀和討論，讓學生理解如何構成一篇引人注目的故事，進而理解如何構成一部好的小說。我們每周讀一至兩篇故事，課程用英語教授。由於本課程是一個研討班課程，積極參與課堂討論是不可缺少的。每位學生必須做兩次口頭報告，並提交一份10頁的期末報告，這份報告可以從口頭報告中延伸出來。",
    "describe_eh": "This course aims to help graduate students build up a solid grounding in reading and analyzing short stories critically. It is hoped that through an intensive reading and discussion of short fiction, students can acquire a better understanding of what constitutes a compelling story and, by extension, a good novel. We will read one or two stories a week, and the class will be conducted in English. As the course is a seminar, active participation in classroom discussion is essential. Each student is required to do two oral presentations and submit a ten-page final term paper, which can be developed out of either oral presentation.",
